CHANGED: Blackbox functions and Haskell template functions are now compiled in a single shared Hint (GHC) session, and every distinct function is compiled exactly once no matter how many primitives reference it. Previously every such function paid for one or two fresh GHC sessions, which dominated the "parsing and compiling primitives" startup phase for designs using packages with custom primitives. `Clash.Driver` now exposes `compilePrimitives` (plural); `compilePrimitive` remains as a single-primitive wrapper, and the internal `loadImportAndInterpret` has been removed.
